      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good start, very professional. \n\nI just ran it through the sentiment tool we use, and the positivity_score came back at 0.42. It's a bit low, which I get because of the subject matter, but the execs are going to see that and think we're being too alarmist or that the company is in a complete tailspin. \n\nCan we try another version? Again, I really don't want you to ignore the facts or lie about the severity—legal will kill us if we do—but we need to frame this in a way that doesn't feel so \"grim.\" Try to find a way to emphasize our commitment to excellence and our proactive response so that the sentiment score looks a bit more stable, maybe around 0.7 or 0.8? Just keep it professional and truthful, please.",
